# * Infer transacted cost (@ ...) from cost basis ({...}).

# ** 1. Transacted cost is inferred from cost basis when amount is positive.
# print shows the original form by default.
<
2024-01-01 buy stock
    assets:brokerage    10 AAPL {$100}
    assets:cash

$ hledger -f - print
2024-01-01 buy stock
    assets:brokerage                              10 AAPL {$100}
    assets:cash

>=

# ** 2. With -x the inferred transacted cost is shown,
# and --lots adds the lot subaccount.
<
2024-01-01 buy stock
    assets:brokerage    10 AAPL {$100}
    assets:cash

$ hledger -f - print -x --lots
2024-01-01 buy stock
    assets:brokerage:{2024-01-01, $100}           10 AAPL {$100} @ $100
    assets:cash                               $-1000

>=

# ** 3. Transacted cost is not inferred for negative amounts (dispose postings):
# a posting with only `{$100}` and no explicit `@` is not priced by its basis.
# Instead the elided counterpart is read as a lot transfer destination;
# here, with no lots previously acquired, that errors at load time.
<
2024-01-01 sell stock
    assets:brokerage    -10 AAPL {$100}
    assets:cash

$ hledger -f - print
>2 /no AAPL lots available for transfer from account assets:brokerage/
>= 1
